    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1538">

                <pb facs="0988" n="872" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg872"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/63a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Special Agent Canova.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-22T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 22, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Proceed to Zacatecas and exert every energy to secure full information especially
                    regarding reported death of two French priests and imprisonment of eleven others
                    and generally regarding treatment accorded to representatives of all religious
                    orders. Telegraph results. Forward mail description conditions since the attack
                    on and fall of Zacatecas, covering treatment accorded foreigners and their
                    interests.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
